# user_data.sh — outline only, no implementation yet.
#
# This runs automatically on the VM's first boot (Terraform hands it to
# the instance as cloud-init data). Roughly, in order:
#
#   1. install Docker + Docker Compose on the VM
#   2. fetch the secrets (DB password, JWT key) from OCI Vault via the
#      OCI CLI — per the blueprint, these were generated by Terraform
#      and written to Vault, never passed in as plain user_data
#   3. write those fetched values into an env file the containers will
#      read (look up: how docker compose's env_file directive expects
#      that file to look)
#   4. get the app onto the VM — either pull pre-built images from a
#      registry, or pull/copy the repo and build locally on the VM
#      (undecided — see Open decisions in the blueprint if it's still
#      open, otherwise whatever you land on)
#   5. docker compose up -d
#
# Worth checking: this script runs as root during cloud-init, with no
# interactive terminal — anything that would normally prompt for
# confirmation needs a flag to run non-interactively.
